5,1,1,talk,Midori,,Hello everyone. I think it's important we identify where our previous projects have struggled. I'm particularly interested in how we handle outages and how our plans evolve after the initial rollout. What do you all think?,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. We need to ensure the new system is compatible with our actual physical environment. I'm concerned about how new software interacts with our aging yard equipment and our peak-season constraints.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,May,,I'm with you both. I want to make sure we aren't just buying a shiny new toy that will rot in three years or leave us cleaning up a mess from external contractors. Let's dig into the history.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Misaki,,I agree. We should also consider the human element. I'm concerned about the burden on our staff during transitions. We need to know how previous rollouts actually affected the people on the ground.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are all in agreement on the need for a forensic approach. While operational stability is key, I believe we must also scrutinize the financial trail to ensure we aren't blindsided by lingering costs.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji @Misaki, your points about the physical environment and staff burden are so important. To understand accountability and adaptability, I'm thinking of looking into support ownership during the outage and the depot supervisors' experience.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, those are good choices. To address the physical risks, I'll look into the yard devices and the 2021 scheduling trial, as well as the depot calendar and the peak-season cutover. We can't afford a failure during peak.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,May,,I'll focus on the upgrade history of the dispatch tool and the data lift in the 2018 pay move. I want to see if we have a habit of letting things decay or botched migrations.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Midori, thank you. I want to see how we've managed our people. I'll look into administrator retirements and hiring times, as well as the depot supervisors and the last rollout.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"A prudent selection. To ensure our financial projections aren't merely optimistic fantasies, I shall examine the board minutes on capital and operating requests, along with five years of renewal invoices. Let's see where the money actually goes.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Midori,,"It seems we have a very comprehensive plan. By covering the financial, technical, and human aspects, we should get a clear picture of the risks. Does anyone feel we've missed a critical area before we finalize?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I believe we have covered the primary bases. As long as we can correlate the financial data with the operational realities of the yard, we should be able to spot the red flags.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,May,,"I think we're set. I'm curious to see if our ""successes"" were actually just patched-up disasters. Let's get to the digging and see who's been hiding what.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Misaki,,I agree. I hope the records show whether our staff were supported or simply left to struggle. I'm ready to proceed with the investigation.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. It is often the footnotes and the ""miscellaneous"" columns that tell the most honest stories. I look forward to seeing if our historical spending aligns with our perceived successes. I am ready.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Midori,,I agree. Let's move forward with these choices. I'll focus on the support ownership during last winter's outage and the depot supervisors and the last rollout. I'm looking forward to hearing what you all find.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I am also ready. I will focus on the yard devices and the 2021 scheduling trial, and the depot calendar and the peak-season cutover. Let's see if the data reflects the reality of the floor.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,May,,"I'm all set. I'll be diving into the upgrade history of the dispatch tool and the data lift in the 2018 pay move. Let's see if we've been playing a dangerous game of ""patch and pray.""","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Misaki,,"I will focus on administrator retirements and hiring times, and the depot supervisors and the last rollout. I want to see if we have the capacity to handle another change.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,"My choices are finalized: the board minutes on capital and operating requests, and five years of renewal invoices. I shall see if our financial history is a straight line or a labyrinth of surprises.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
