58,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Looking at the options, Anchor Industrial Software seems most promising. Having an engineering team present through rollout addresses my concerns about accountability and ensures the plan actually sticks with the staff on the ground.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,I agree with @Midori. Anchor's on-site engineering team is the only way to ensure the system survives our fragmented hardware and the chaos of peak season. They can adapt to the yard's reality in real-time.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, @Midori, you're falling for the ""on-site"" charm. Anchor puts it on our own servers—that's just a recipe for another fossil that we'll be too scared to update in five years. We need a hosted solution.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@May, I understand the risk of technical debt, but we cannot ignore our staffing crisis. With our administrators retiring, we don't have the internal capacity to manage a hosted migration alone. Anchor's on-site presence is a lifeline.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, while I share your distaste for fossils, @Misaki's point on staffing is valid. However, we must look at the billing. Corvus is a nightmare of separate licenses; it is the very labyrinth of costs I fear.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, I agree that Corvus is too risky. @May, while I hear your concerns about fossils, a hosted suite like Meridian might be too rigid. Anchor's on-site team provides the accountability we've been missing.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, a hosted suite like Meridian or Tessera is a gamble if the interface doesn't play nice with our old scanners. Anchor's engineers can troubleshoot the hardware on the spot, which is the only way to avoid paper dispatch.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, that's just a band-aid. If we go with Anchor, we're just paying engineers to prop up a sinking ship on our own racks. Meridian's hosted suite is the only way to stop the decay.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, a hosted suite is only a solution if the people can actually use it. If we lack the staff to manage the transition, the most modern system will still be abandoned by the crews. Anchor is the safest choice for our people.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, @Misaki, we are weighing technical purity against human capacity. However, let us consider Meridian. A fixed configuration and a regional service team suggest a predictability in both function and cost that Anchor's bespoke on-site engineering may lack.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, predictability is good, but a ""fixed configuration"" might be exactly what leads to the depots abandoning the system again. We need the flexibility and accountability that Anchor's on-site team provides to ensure it actually works.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Benjamin, predictability is useless if the system crashes during peak because it wasn't tuned to our yard. Anchor's on-site engineers can ensure the software actually functions on our hardware before the rush hits.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, you're obsessed with the yard, but I'm obsessed with the next decade. Anchor is just a fancy way of saying ""we'll build you a custom cage."" Meridian's hosted model is the only way to ensure we don't end up with another fossil.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, a ""custom cage"" is better than a system no one knows how to use. We are losing our experts. Anchor's on-site team provides the direct support our exhausted staff desperately needs to survive this change.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, your vision of the future is admirable, but @Misaki and @Ryuji's concerns are immediate. If we must choose, Anchor's on-site presence offers a tangible safeguard, provided the contract prevents the ""bespoke"" nature from becoming a financial sinkhole.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May"",""Misaki"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Midori,,I believe we've found our balance. Anchor Industrial Software provides the accountability and hands-on support we need to prevent another outage and ensure the staff actually adopts the system. I'm voting for Anchor.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. The risk of returning to paper dispatch is too high to ignore. Anchor is the only choice that addresses our hardware fragmentation and peak-season constraints with real-world engineering. I vote for Anchor.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,I'm the only one thinking about the long game here. Anchor is just a polished version of the same mistakes we've made for years. I can't support another on-premise fossil. I vote for Meridian.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I cannot risk another failed rollout that leaves our remaining staff overwhelmed. We need the direct, on-site support that only Anchor provides to bridge our knowledge gap. I vote for Anchor.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"While I maintain a healthy skepticism of on-premise installations, the consensus on operational survival is overwhelming. Provided we lock in the pricing to avoid hidden fees, Anchor is the logical choice. I vote for Anchor.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
